  "details": "When a particle from an avatar's ParticleSystem collides with a world collider,\n\nOnParticleCollision(GameObject other) fires, but `other` is null because avatar\n\nobjects are protected. World creators therefore cannot tell which player the\n\nparticle came from.\n\nTest (SDK 3.10.5, live client, local avatar, collision module + Send Collision Messages):\n\n- Two world targets, 5 shots each from an avatar gun\n\n- Raw events: 10, other == null: 10, non-null: 0\n\n- The existing Player-routing path did not trigger (Player events: 0)\n\nUse case: PvP worlds where players bring their own avatar guns. Hits can be\n\ndetected, but kills cannot be attributed to a shooter. Workarounds (estimating\n\ntrajectories from hand bone poses) break down for arcing or exploding projectiles.\n\nProposal: when an avatar's particle collides with a world object, keep `other`\n\nhidden as it is now, but raise a new event such as\n\nOnAvatarParticleCollision(VRCPlayerApi owner) that only exposes the owning player.\n\nThis follows the same approach already used for player triggers and collisions:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/udon/p/ontriggerenter-event-gives-a-null-reference-if-a-player-enters-the-collider\n\nNo avatar objects or components are exposed, so it should not create ripping\n\nor manipulation risks.",
